return {
    ["        很久没有再写日记了，在这个黑暗的陵寝中，在疯狂与污染交织的缝隙里，清醒是困难的。\n        回首这一生，我从一个普通的穿越者，变成了改变世界的大帝。我发明了蒸汽机，建立了共和国，征服了海洋，书写了法律……但我也失去了太多——我的故乡，我的平凡，我的孩子们的爱，还有……我自己。\n        黄涛，你还记得吗？那个在地球上熬夜看小说、打游戏、抱怨工作的普通青年？那个想念妈妈做的红烧肉、想念和朋友撸串吹牛的普通人？有时候我觉得自己好像做了一个很长的梦，梦里我成为了无所不能的大帝，但醒来时，我只想要一张回家的车票。\n        但我知道，我回不去了。即使成为真神，即使拥有改变一切的力量，我也回不去那个有网络、有外卖、有平凡幸福的家了。\n        所以，我只能把这里当成我的家，把这个世界当成我另一个的家乡。\n        我留下了蒸汽机，留下了法律，留下了航道，留下了故事和诗歌……我希望这个世界能变得更好，希望后来的人能少受一些苦，希望他们能记住——曾经有一个人，从很远的地方来，把这里当成了自己的家。\n        贝尔纳黛，如果你能看到这份日记，我想告诉你：爸爸不是一个好皇帝，也不是一个好父亲。我做出了太多错误的选择，伤害了太多我爱的人。但如果重来一次，我还是会选择保护你，哪怕你看不到，哪怕你恨我。\n        还有夏尔、博诺瓦……我的孩子们。愿你们能在这个我亲手改变过的世界里，找到属于自己的幸福。\n        我也许又要沉眠了。我不知道，哪一次道别，会成为真正的告别。但不要悲伤。我，罗塞尔·古斯塔夫，黄涛——即使死亡，也要死得轰轰烈烈！况且……谁说我真的死了呢？\n        只要还有人记得我的名字，只要我的故事还在流传，只要这个世界还在使用我留下的发明和律法……我就从未真正离开。等着吧，总有一天，你们会听到那句话——\n        因蒂斯的子民们，你们的皇帝，回来了！"] = "It has been a long time since I wrote in my diary. In this dark mausoleum, in the gaps where madness and corruption intertwine, clarity is difficult. \n Looking back on this life, I went from an ordinary transmigrator to an Emperor who changed the world. I invented the steam engine, established the Republic, conquered the oceans, wrote the laws... but I also lost too much—my hometown, my ordinariness, the love of my children, and... myself. \n Huang Tao, do you remember? That ordinary young man on Earth who stayed up late reading novels, playing games, and complaining about work? That ordinary person who missed the braised pork made by his mom and missed hanging out with friends to eat skewers and brag? Sometimes I feel like I had a very long dream, in which I became an omnipotent Emperor, but when I wake up, I only want a ticket home. \n But I know, I can't go back. Even if I become a True God, even if I possess the power to change everything, I can't go back to that home with the internet, takeout, and ordinary happiness. \n So, I can only treat this place as my home and this world as my other hometown. \n I left behind the steam engine, the laws, the shipping routes, the stories, and the poems... I hope this world can become better, I hope later generations can suffer less, and I hope they can remember—there was once a person who came from very far away and treated this place as his own home. \n Bernadette, if you can see this diary, I want to tell you: Dad is not a good Emperor, nor is he a good father. I made too many wrong choices and hurt too many people I loved. But if I could do it all over again, I would still choose to protect you, even if you can't see it, even if you hate me. \n And Charles, Bernadette... my children. May you find your own happiness in this world that I changed with my own hands. \n I might have to sleep again. I don't know which farewell will be the real one. But don't be sad. I, Roselle Gustav, Huang Tao—even if I die, I will die with a bang! Besides... who said I really died? \n As long as there is still someone who remembers my name, as long as my story is still being told, as long as this world is still using the inventions and laws I left behind... I have never truly left. Just wait, one day, you will hear that sentence— \n Citizens of Intis, your Emperor has returned!",
